From ff04a6feab1cb64ec8f3fd6fde95cf4982aded6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: l4h <z@univalence.me>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 10:20:48 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] x86/vcpu: VT-x guest accesses to CR8 always exit

CR8 is the core's local APIC TPR.  Without the TPR shadow, which 0039
does not allow, and with CR8-load and CR8-store exiting clear, a guest
MOV to or from CR8 reaches the TPR itself.  Nothing switches the TPR at
VM entry or exit, and seL4 never writes it, so:

- the next guest on the core reads the value the last one left there;
- a guest that raises it masks the host's interrupts on that core: those
  at or below the TPR's priority class are no longer delivered, so
  neither the host's timer nor its IPIs end guest mode, and they stay
  masked for seL4 and every thread after it.

So, as with MOV-DR (0039), CR8-load and CR8-store exiting are always on.
A guest's MOV to or from CR8 is a control-register exit to userspace,
which emulates CR8 per VCPU.  Reading back the primary controls shows
both bits set.  AMD-V (0040) needs no counterpart: V_INTR_MASKING is
always on, so a guest's CR8 is its VMCB's V_TPR.
---
 src/arch/x86/object/vcpu.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/arch/x86/object/vcpu.c b/src/arch/x86/object/vcpu.c
index 94dd0da38..d9b8b9ad6 100644
--- a/src/arch/x86/object/vcpu.c
+++ b/src/arch/x86/object/vcpu.c
@@ -287,6 +287,8 @@ static bool_t BOOT_CODE init_vtx_fixed_values(bool_t useTrueMsrs)
     uint32_t primary_control_mask =
         BIT(10) |   //MWAIT exiting
         BIT(11) |   //RDPMC exiting: the counters are not switched
+        BIT(19) |   //CR8-load exiting: CR8 is the core's APIC TPR
+        BIT(20) |   //CR8-store exiting
         BIT(23) |   //MOV-DR exiting: neither are the debug registers
         BIT(25) |   //Use I/O bitmaps
         BIT(28) |   //Use MSR bitmaps
